  "title": "Oodgeroo Noonuccal",
  "summary": "A Quandamooka activist, poet, writer and educator, born on Minjerribah (North Stradbroke Island). Her 1964 book We Are Going made her the first Aboriginal woman to publish a book of poetry. She opened her home Moongalba as a cultural education centre, returned her MBE in 1987 in protest at the bicentenary, and died in 1993 on her ancestral land.",
